---
import LegalPage from "../../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { PROPERTY_ASSISTANT as P } from "../../data/products";
import { SELLER as S, POLICY_LINKS as L } from "../../data/seller";
---

<LegalPage
  title={`${P.name}: subscription and trial terms`}
  description={`Terms for the free trial and the Assistant plan of ${P.name}: what you get, the price, billing, renewal, cancelling and what happens to your data. Sold by ${S.legalName}.`}
>
  <h1>{P.name}: subscription and trial terms</h1>
  <p class="updated">Version 2026-11. Last updated: 24 November 2026</p>

  <p class="note">
    These terms cover the free trial and the Assistant plan of {P.name}.
    The seller is <strong>{S.legalName}</strong>; {S.brand} is its brand. Refunds are explained in the
    <a href={L.refunds}>refund and cancellation policy</a>, personal data in the
    <a href={L.privacy}>privacy notice</a>, and how to reach us on the <a href={L.contact}>contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who the agreement is between</h2>
  <p>
    The agreement is between {S.legalName} ({S.address}; {S.corporationNo}), which trades as {S.brand}
    ("we"), and the real-estate business that requests a trial or subscribes ("you", "your office").
    The service is for businesses only. It is not sold to consumers. The person who signs up confirms that
    they may do so for the office.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What the service is</h2>
  <p>
    We read the public pages of your office's website (your listings and your guides) and build an AI
    assistant from them. The assistant answers questions about your listings and guides in plain language
    and shows the listing or page each answer comes from. We call the stored copy of your pages your office's
    "brain".
  </p>

  <h2>3. The free trial</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Length and price.</strong> 14 days, free. We do not ask for a payment card for the trial.</li>
    <li><strong>What you get.</strong> Your office's brain built from up to 300 listings, the chatbot on a
      private link with up to 50 visitor questions, the connection for your team's Claude or ChatGPT, one
      listing brief, up to 5 listing videos of your own listings, and the result of our 200-question test.</li>
    <li><strong>When it starts.</strong> We build the trial after we receive your request and aim to send it
      within 24 hours on working days. The 14 days start on the day we send it to you.</li>
    <li><strong>When it ends.</strong> The trial stops by itself after 14 days. Nothing is charged, and it
      does not turn into a paid subscription unless you choose to subscribe.</li>
    <li><strong>Conditions.</strong> One trial per office. We need your website address and a work e-mail
      address at your agency. We may decline or stop a trial, for example if we cannot confirm that the request
      comes from the office, or if the website is not a real-estate agency's.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. The Assistant plan</h2>
  <p>The Assistant plan is the paid subscription. For one office it includes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the chatbot for your own website;</li>
    <li>up to 500 listings in your office's brain, re-read every day;</li>
    <li>up to 1,500 visitor questions a month;</li>
    <li>5 listing briefs a month, each sent to you for approval first;</li>
    <li>every enquiry that a visitor leaves with the chatbot, sent to your office by e-mail;</li>
    <li>the connection for your team's Claude or ChatGPT;</li>
    <li>a monthly report on what visitors asked.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    "One office" means one website and its listings, and everyone who works there. There is no fee per agent.
    To use the assistant inside Claude or ChatGPT, each person needs their own Claude or ChatGPT account on a
    plan that allows custom connectors; that account is covered by your agreement with its provider, not by
    these terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    If your office regularly needs more listings or more visitor questions than the plan includes, we contact
    you to agree a larger plan. We do not charge anything extra without your agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Other packages and add-ons</h2>
  <p>
    We also offer the Marketing and Lead Desk packages, the
    voice agent add-on, and CRM (customer relationship management system) integration. These are not part of
    the Assistant plan and cannot be bought by card on this website. We sell them by written quote and a
    separate agreement. The voice agent add-on is sold with a 12-month contract. Parts marked "In build" or "Pilot" on the product page are not available yet.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Price and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Price.</strong> USD 99 (US dollars) a month for each office.</li>
    <li><strong>Taxes.</strong> The price does not include taxes. If a sales tax applies to your purchase, it
      is shown before you pay.</li>
    <li><strong>How you pay.</strong> By payment card, on a secure payment page run by our payment provider,
      Stripe. Your card details go to Stripe. We do not see or store your full card number.</li>
    <li><strong>When you pay.</strong> The first payment is taken on the day you subscribe and covers the month
      that starts that day. You get a receipt by e-mail for every payment.</li>
    <li><strong>Card statement.</strong> The payment appears on your statement as
      the name of our company, BioInsight Lab Inc., or our brand, LeadFlow.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Renewal</h2>
  <p>
    The subscription runs month to month. It renews automatically on the same day of each month, and the card
    you gave is charged USD 99 for the next month, until you cancel. There is no minimum term.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Cancelling</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel at any time. E-mail <a href={`mailto:${S.supportEmail}`}>{S.supportEmail}</a> from an address
    at your office and say that you want to cancel. We confirm by e-mail within 24 hours on working days.
  </p>
  <p>
    The cancellation counts from the moment your e-mail arrives. No further payment is taken. Your assistant
    keeps working until the end of the month you have already paid for, then it is switched off. Refunds are
    explained in the <a href={L.refunds}>refund and cancellation policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. If a payment fails</h2>
  <p>
    If a renewal payment fails, we tell you by e-mail and the payment is tried again. If it is still unpaid
    14 days after the renewal date, we switch the assistant off and end the subscription. You owe nothing for
    the time after it is switched off.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to the price or the plan</h2>
  <p>
    If we change the price or reduce what the plan includes, we tell you by e-mail at least 15 calendar days before the
    change. The change applies from your next renewal after those 15 days. If you do not agree, you can cancel
    before it applies.
  </p>

  <h2>11. How the service is delivered</h2>
  <p>
    The service is digital. Nothing is shipped. We deliver by e-mail to the work address you gave us: the
    private link to the chatbot, the connector address for Claude and ChatGPT, the test result and your
    listing briefs. For the Assistant plan we also send what your web developer needs to place the chatbot on
    your website. When you subscribe, nothing has to be delivered again: the assistant from your trial stays on,
    and the plan is switched on automatically as soon as your first payment succeeds.
  </p>

  <h2>12. An AI assistant can make mistakes</h2>
  <p>
    The assistant is an AI system. It is built to answer only from your published listings and pages, to show
    the source, and to decline when your website does not cover the question. It can still give a wrong or
    incomplete answer. Visitors are told that they are talking to an AI assistant. The assistant does not give
    legal, tax, financial or valuation advice, and it does not replace your agents.
  </p>
  <p>
    You remain responsible for your listings, your prices and what your office tells buyers and owners. We
    send each listing brief to you first; you decide whether it goes out. Tell us about a wrong answer and we
    correct the cause as soon as we reasonably can.
  </p>

  <h2>13. No promised results</h2>
  <p>
    We do not promise any number of enquiries, leads, viewings or sales. We work to keep the service
    running, but we do not promise that it will be available without interruption.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Your content</h2>
  <p>
    Your listings, guides, photos and documents stay yours. You confirm that your office may publish them, and
    you allow us to read and copy them to build and run your assistant. We use them only for your office. The
    listing briefs, videos and reports we make for you are yours to use.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Personal data</h2>
  <p>
    We use the contact details you give us to build and send your trial, to run your subscription and to
    answer you, as described in the <a href={L.privacy}>privacy notice</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    During the trial the chatbot does not collect visitors' contact details; it shows your office's. On the
    Assistant plan, when a visitor leaves contact details with the chatbot, we pass them to your office and
    use them for nothing else. For those details your office decides why and how they are used, and we handle
    them on your behalf, under data processing terms that we give you before you subscribe. We use hosting
    and AI model providers to run the service; the data processing terms name them.
  </p>

  <h2>16. Your data when the trial or the subscription ends</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>End of a trial.</strong> If you do not subscribe, the chatbot link and the connector stop
      working when the trial ends. We delete your office's brain and the questions asked during the trial within
      30 days.</li>
    <li><strong>End of a subscription.</strong> The assistant is switched off at the end of the month you paid
      for. Within 30 days after that we delete your office's brain, the questions visitors asked and any
      visitor details held for your office.</li>
    <li><strong>Sooner on request.</strong> Ask us by e-mail and we delete this data within 7 days.</li>
    <li><strong>A copy for you.</strong> Ask before the deletion and we send you the monthly reports and the
      enquiries we hold for your office.</li>
    <li><strong>What we keep.</strong> Your office's name and contact address, and the records of payments, for
      as long as our accounts and the law require.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>17. Acceptable use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the service only for your own office's website and listings.</li>
    <li>Do not use it for anything unlawful, or to publish listings or statements that mislead buyers.</li>
    <li>Follow the rules on property advertising and on data protection that apply to your office.</li>
    <li>Do not resell the service, share your private links outside your office, or try to break or overload
      the service.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If these rules are broken we may switch the assistant off. Where the problem can be fixed, we tell you
    first and give you a reasonable time to fix it.
  </p>

  <h2>18. Legal restrictions</h2>
  <p>
    We do not provide the service to persons or organisations under Canadian, United States, European Union or
    United Kingdom sanctions, or in countries where those sanctions forbid it.
  </p>

  <h2>19. If we end the subscription</h2>
  <p>
    We may end a subscription by giving you at least 30 days' notice by e-mail. If we do, or if we stop
    offering the service, we refund the part of your last payment that covers the time after the service stops.
  </p>

  <h2>20. No warranty and liability</h2>
  <p>
    The service is provided as is. Neither side is liable to the other for indirect or consequential losses,
    including lost profits or lost sales. Each side's total liability under these terms is limited to the
    amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. These limits do not apply to liability that cannot
    be limited by law, such as for fraud.
  </p>

  <h2>21. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    If these terms change, we tell you by e-mail at least 15 calendar days before the new version applies. If you do
    not agree, you can cancel before it applies.
  </p>

  <h2>22. Law and courts</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada that apply
    there, and the courts of Ontario decide any dispute. This does not take away rights you have under the
    data protection law that applies to you.
  </p>

  <h2>23. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {S.legalName}, {S.address}. Customer service: <a href={`mailto:${S.supportEmail}`}>{S.supportEmail}</a>.
    More on the <a href={L.contact}>contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
